{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A persistent inspection error prevents later PR changes from being observed, potentially leaving merges, closures, and CI failures unrecorded."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failure that recovers during a main-red pause is permanently omitted from the failure ledger."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid repository spelling with different casing prevents CI failures from being classified or rerun."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"If a later partial attempt omits the tracked job, the reproduced reconciliation logic leaves its earlier successful rerun unresolved; the fixture did not verify GitHub's live response behavior."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rerun outside the first 100 observed contexts can finish without another inspection, leaving its outcome unrecorded indefinitely."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A normal Node test timeout is reported as needing a fix instead of receiving the requested transient rerun."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A standard Playwright failure heading bypasses the security-test exclusion and allows the job to be rerun and recorded."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Repeated inspection during a main-red pause consumes API quota and postpones mergeability nudges and access-problem recovery."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A stale persisted push marker after a crash can hide a remote PR closure and other observations until the marker clears."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rate-limited rerun request remains pending across polls and restart, preventing both retry and a needs-fix result."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Lagging check data can generate a needs-fix item for a failure whose rerun has already passed, prompting unnecessary work."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Multiple failing checks generate separate main-red feed items for the same repository episode."},{"id":"C13","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failing legacy status on main can be missed when the PR uses a check run, causing a rerun that should have been paused."},{"id":"C14","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A CI failure first observed as a PR closes can be reported in the feed without being classified or recorded."},{"id":"C15","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rerun ending neutral or skipped remains pending indefinitely and never receives a terminal ledger outcome."},{"id":"C16","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The feed excerpt can show setup output instead of failure context, although the selected failure remains in the signature."},{"id":"C17","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Setup text can become the failure signature, conflating unrelated failures and undermining ledger-based decisions."},{"id":"C21","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unrelated name such as disaster is classified as security-related, suppressing both the timeout rerun and ledger entry."},{"id":"C22","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Fail-fast cancellations can be rerun and recorded as flakes even though a sibling's deterministic failure caused them."},{"id":"C6b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An untimestamped indented Playwright timeout is reported as needing a fix instead of being rerun."},{"id":"C7b","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A standard Go security-test failure heading bypasses the exclusion and allows the job to be rerun and recorded."}]}